			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844348">
									

<p>this is a pretty solid idea for a memetic kill agent, but I feel like it being THE kill agent for the foundation wouldn't make much sense. It seems like there are multiple memetic kill agents used (scp 1 and scp 2000), so it would be odd for the foundation to let anyone with access to any scp with a kill agent to have access to scp 1. furthermore, this doesn't seem like a thing that can be deleted with amnestics, so if some researcher of an scp with a kill agent needed to edit the article in any way, they would permanently have access to 1, 2000, and every other kill agent. Maybe the kill agent articles are just incredibly incredibly exclusive, but with experimental logs, I'm not too sure about that. The only other problem I have is that it definitely seems like a big scp, and would be difficult to properly write as a second(I'm assuming second from your submissions) scp. Besides that, this is a really nice idea for how memetic kill agents work (besides the exclusivity bit). I would +1 it if you could figure out a way to circumvent the problems I said above.</p>

