			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844323">
									

<p>1) If this is negotiating with The Foundation specifically, then that means it has some sapience. This may give The Foundation a reason to try and determine if it can work out a better deal. Even if it's just basically an animal, the reason for targeting The Foundation needs to be explored.</p>
<p>2) Along those lines, an MTF or D-Class may be the wrong idea: The Foundation using this as a prison for its own prisoners or as a way to soften up those it interrogates may be a possibility. This would give the apartment its prisoners and give The Foundation a way to make those it arrests useful beyond any information they may otherwise offer.</p>
<p>Of course, there's nothing to say that the apartment could have an exclusive deal.</p>
<p>3) You need to emphasize the maze-like structure of the apartment. The devil's bargain works (prisoner for info/treasure) but you need to emphasize how hard it is to escape. That would create a much scarier location.</p>
<p>Otherwise, great idea! And your English isn't that bad.</p>

