														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844308">
									

<p>I like this one, especially because of the binary option, but there are some problems:</p>
<p>1) I'm guessing that if you flick it off it takes your personality, if you flick it on you gain all currently absorbed personalities. This is fine, but you may want to put a limit on that if you have multiple personalities in your head only your personality is absorbed and the others are lost. Otherwise, you could potentially have a ridiculous number of personalities.</p>
<p>2) What are the relative strengths of the personalities? Basically, is there a struggle for control, and what kind of power do the other personalities have regarding the actions of the body? Also, are the personalities relegated to the back and can only watch or do they have any kind of voice in what happens?</p>
<p>3) What happens if you flick it on but it doesn't have a personality? What happens if the personality was already given to someone else? Could you absorb another personality and that personality resurrect the body, albeit under new management?</p>
<p>4) While I like the concept, the corpse personality drain may be one step too far. That's the only thing I would suggest dropping.</p>
<p>5) Strictly as a side note, the multiple personalities may actually make the Bookkeeper easier to threaten. Not only is he the receptacle of multiple lives, and thus making him more willing to make a deal; the more personalities the easier he would be to threaten. Also, the personalities may break and at least debate a deal, meaning that the weakest personality would determine if the person breaks.</p>
<p>But otherwise, great concept!</p>

							</div>

								
					
