			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844293">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Conventional, with containment procedures and description followed by supplemental incident reports and experimental logs. This is followed by a &quot;secret&quot; file with restricted access.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The source of all memetic kill agents used by the foundation, as well as the means of inoculation. A species of coral emits a cognitohazardous vibration that forces cardiac arrest in observers. This vibration remains hazardous in any data form. Polyps separate from the coral and enter an animal's brain, whereupon it becomes immune to the cognitohazard. All high ranking officials of the Foundation are hosting a brain parasite. This coral has formed a symbiotic relationship with the entire foundation. This means YOU have the parasite if you've ever survived the SCP-001 kill agent.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The unique effects of the cognitohazard vibration are discovered when security workers are killed viewing the waveform of security footage. Research into its properties and the extent of this effect is undergone. At some point, the idea to use it for security was proposed by the heads of research, Dr. Berryman and Langford, and publicly denied. Shortly after, an &quot;incident&quot; on-site causes the &quot;death&quot; of all coral bushes. In reality, they are quietly moved to an unknown location to implement the memetic security agent.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> My idea is that the true nature of the SCP is hinted at throughout the text before being revealed at the end. The Neutralized classification and description of its supposed destruction should hopefully be somewhat intriguing.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> No idea if this conflicts with any previous articles. As this is my first work and it attempts to retcon something so iconic it may be controversial.</p>
<p>The idea is that the coral will only infect animals that choose not to feed on it, and releases a vibration pulse that travels far underwater and kills all others. This poses the question of what benefit the coral would receive from not simply killing everything around it. Maybe by &quot;whitelisting&quot; certain animals, it can manipulate its ecosystem to evolve beneficially.</p>
<p>Also not sure how the parasite would get in your brain. It would need to enter in a way as to not cause any long-term damage if any at all.</p>
<p>SCP-3000 has proven that the Foundation will utilize anomalies to their benefit, although that is arguably less extreme.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
